@schema medical.core
@title Core EMS/Medical Protocol Schema
@version 1.0
@description Defines standard tags used in emergency and prehospital care protocols. Enables AI-assisted parsing, validation, and retrieval of medical procedures, medications, and workflows.
@created 2025-05-04
@created_by Mike (FolkTech AI)
@license MIT

@required
- @protocol              # Unique ID for the protocol block (machine-parseable)
- @title                 # Human-readable title
- @end                   # Must be used to close each @protocol block

@optional
- @agency                # EMS or hospital system name
- @region                # Geographic service area
- @last_updated          # Last revised date (YYYY-MM-DD)
- @indications           # When to apply the protocol
- @contraindications     # When NOT to apply the protocol
- @procedure             # Step-by-step actions
- @medications           # Drug names, doses, routes, etc.
- @notes                 # Cautions, additional info, field notes
- @references            # Source material or medical guidelines
- @ai_note               # Metadata for AI use (tags, token cost, RAG relevance)
- @tags                  # Freeform tags for categorization/search

@notes
- Only blocks explicitly listed in `@required` need `@end`
- Tags inside blocks should only appear once unless future schemas allow repeat
- List-style values must begin with `- `
- Tags must start at the line beginning and use `@tag` format
- Tags may include alphanumeric characters, periods, and underscores only
@end
